    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191306": {
      "title": "Full-time, Tenured or Tenure-track Faculty Positions in the Accounting & Control Area",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Full-time, Tenured or Tenure-track Faculty Positions in the Accounting & Control Area INSEAD Location France, Singapore Open Date Sep 03, 2026 Deadline Nov 01, 2026 at 11:59 PM Eastern Time Description INSEAD invites applications for full-time, tenured or tenure-track faculty positions in the Accounting & Control Area, to begin in September 2027. We are recruiting at all levels. We will consider applications for either our Fontainebleau or Singapore campuses. If you have a campus preference, please state this in your cover letter. We are seeking individuals with high levels of achievement and/or outstanding promise in research and teaching. Qualifications Applications are welcome from PhD students in accounting or related fields. Interested candidates should apply via INSEAD’s Interfolio if they are interested in being interviewed. INSEAD will attend the EAA Talent Workshop in Madrid in November 2026 and will conduct first-round interviews there, but also on Zoom for candidates that cannot attend the EAA Talent Workshop . Full-time faculty position is either tenured or tenure track. Decisions about incoming status and promotion are based on performance, principally in research and teaching. INSEAD salaries are competitive with those of the top US schools; research support and annual teaching loads are comparable. INSEAD is recognised as one of the world’s leading business schools. This includes recognition as the 3rd MBA programme in the world by the Financial Times in the 3 past year average ranking. The school has two primary campus locations: one in the royal forest of Fontainebleau, which is approximately one hour from Paris, the other in the metropolitan capital of Singapore. There is also a campus in Abu Dhabi that allows for research and teaching opportunities. The school attracts participants from over 75 countries to its MBA, EMBA, executive, and PhD programmes. The Accounting & Control faculty teach in all of these programmes, and we offer our own PhD. Application Instructions Please ensure to apply via INSEAD online application tool: https://apply.interfolio.com/191306 .  Please ensure to provide the email address of all your supervisors so that they can upload your recommendation letters themselves. The due date to submit your package and recommendation letters is 1 November 2026. All applications should include a cover letter, a complete CV, a job market paper, a research and teaching Statement, three recommendation letters, and recent publications/working papers. If you need further information, please contact us at Recruiting.Accounting.Area@insead.edu Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement INSEAD is committed to the principle of equal employment opportunity for all employees and to providing employees with a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at INSEAD are based on business needs, job requirements and individual qualifications, without regard to race, color, religion or belief, gender or sexual orientation, family or parental status, or any other status protected by the laws or regulations in the locations where we operate. INSEAD will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. INSEAD encourages applicants of all ages. Our Data Protection Notice explains how INSEAD uses your personal data and your rights. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Cookie Details List‎ Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Cookie Details List‎ Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. Cookie Details List‎ Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Cookie Details List‎ Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Confirm my choices"
