    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193805": {
      "title": "Full-time tenure-track faculty position in the Decision Sciences Area",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Full-time tenure-track faculty position in the Decision Sciences Area INSEAD: Decision Sciences Location Europe Campus (Fontainebleau, France), Middle East Campus (Abu Dhabi), Asia Campus (Singapore) Open Date Sep 17, 2026 Deadline Oct 25, 2026 at 11:59 PM Eastern Time Description The Decision Sciences (DSC) Area at INSEAD , a global business school with campuses in Abu Dhabi, France, and Singapore, invites applicants for a full-time tenure-track faculty position. The anticipated start date is September 1, 2027. The DSC Area focuses on questions broadly related to individual, group, and organizational decision making, both from behavioral and quantitative perspectives, and with prescriptive, descriptive, and normative approaches. Our research spans decision sciences, judgment and decision making, statistics and machine learning, artificial intelligence and computer science, psychology, economics, operations research, optimization, neuroscience, finance, marketing, organizational behavior, social innovation, and entrepreneurship. We have a collegial environment that encourages interdisciplinary and practically relevant, impactful research. Qualifications We are interested in candidates who can further enrich, expand, and consolidate the diverse research portfolio of the area and the school. This year, we are particularly interested in candidates with expertise at the intersection of computational social science, psychology, and statistics. Applicants should have a Ph.D. or be at the dissertation completion stage of a doctoral program and have a strong research track record and scholarly potential in decision sciences and/or human decision making at the intrapersonal, interpersonal, organizational or macro levels of analysis. Demonstrated experience in teaching effectively is a plus. The position entails the following responsibilities: research in areas of expertise and interest; teaching in INSEAD programs; supervision of doctoral candidates; and service to the school and the broader community. Salary is competitive. Application Instructions For full consideration, please submit a cover letter, a curriculum vitae, research and teaching statements, representative research papers, teaching evaluations if available, and three letters of recommendation no later than October 25, 2026, 11:59 PM Eastern Time. If you have any further questions, please contact insead.DSC-area@insead.edu . Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement INSEAD is committed to the principle of equal employment opportunity for all employees and to providing employees with a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at INSEAD are based on business needs, job requirements and individual qualifications, without regard to race, color, religion or belief, gender or sexual orientation, family or parental status, or any other status protected by the laws or regulations in the locations where we operate. INSEAD will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. INSEAD encourages applicants of all ages. Our Data Protection Notice explains how INSEAD uses your personal data and your rights. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content