    "https://apply.interfolio.com/157066": {
      "title": "Full-time, tenured, or tenure-track faculty positions in the Finance Area24",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Full-time, tenured, or tenure-track faculty positions in the Finance Area24 INSEAD: Finance Location Fontainebleau, France or Singapore Open Date Oct 14, 2024 Description INSEAD’s Finance Department invites applications for faculty positions at all levels (assistant, associate and full) on both Fontainebleau and Singapore campuses. The search is for full-time, tenure track positions starting September 2025. As one of the world's leading and largest graduate business schools, INSEAD offers participants a truly global educational experience. With locations in Europe (France), Asia (Singapore), the Middle East (Abu Dhabi) and North America (San Francisco) and alliances with top institutions, INSEAD's business education and research spans the globe. The school's 162 renowned Faculty members from 40 countries inspire more than 1,300 students in our degree and PhD programmes. In addition, more than 11,000 executives participate in INSEAD's Executive Education programmes each year. Qualifications Candidates should have a strong commitment to produce the highest quality research, publishable in top academic journals and they should demonstrate the ability to teach at the MBA, Master In Management, and PhD levels. They must have a PhD in Finance, Economics, or related disciplines, or expect to complete all requirements for a PhD during the current academic year. Applicants as Associate/Full Professors should have demonstrated research and teaching excellence. Application Instructions Applications should include a cover letter, a complete CV, three letters of recommendation, a job market paper, and any recent publications/working papers. Research and Teaching statements are optional.  Please also specify whether you are interested in Fontainebleau, Singapore, or both. Please submit your application by 18 November 2024 to ensure full consideration. If you need any information, please contact us at insead.FIN-area@insead.edu . Interviews will take place via Zoom at the beginning of December and flyouts will be in person in one of our campuses We value diversity and strongly encourage applications from individuals from all identies and backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from female candidates and members of other underrepresented groups in the field of finance. Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement INSEAD is committed to the principle of equal employment opportunity for all employees and to providing employees with a work environment free of discrimination and harassment. All employment decisions at INSEAD are based on business needs, job requirements and individual qualifications, without regard to race, color, religion or belief, gender or sexual orientation, family or parental status, or any other status protected by the laws or regulations in the locations where we operate. INSEAD will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. INSEAD encourages applicants of all ages. Our Data Protection Notice explains how INSEAD uses your personal data and your rights. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more informat